{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7277303","formula":"C₁₂H₁₇N₃O","hill":"C12H17N3O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":12.0,"H":17.0,"N":3.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"RO5166017"},"descriptions":{"en":"RO5166017, or RO-5166017, is a drug developed by Hoffmann-La Roche which acts as a potent and selective agonist for the trace amine-associated receptor 1 (TAAR1), with no significant activity at other targets. It is a partial agonist or near-full agonist depending on the species. The drug is important for the study of the TAAR1 receptor, as while numerous other compounds are known which act as TAAR1 agonists, such as methamphetamine, MDMA, and 3-iodothyronamine, all previously known TAAR1 agonists are either weak and rapidly metabolized (endogenous ligands), or have strong pharmacological activity at other targets (amphetamines, thyronamines), making it very difficult to assess which effects…"},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":25016538,"mass":219.28,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCN(C[C@H]1COC(=N1)N)C2=CC=CC=C2","inchikey":"PPONHQQJLWPUPH-JTQLQIEISA-N","iupac":"(4S)-4-[(N-ethylanilino)methyl]-4,5-dihydro-1,3-oxazol-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"25016538","atoms":33,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.635,"y":1.294,"z":-0.23,"el":"O"},{"x":0.53,"y":-0.905,"z":-0.324,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.411,"y":-0.464,"z":0.563,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.722,"y":-0.192,"z":1.122,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.504,"y":0.41,"z":-0.196,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.594,"y":-0.416,"z":-1.084,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.424,"y":1.328,"z":-0.972,"el":"C"},{"x":0.499,"y":-2.285,"z":0.166,"el":"C"},{"x":1.645,"y":-0.095,"z":-0.061,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.551,"y":0.154,"z":0.517,"el":"C"},{"x":1.291,"y":-3.187,"z":-0.761,"el":"C"},{"x":1.683,"y":1.215,"z":-0.538,"el":"C"},{"x":2.716,"y":-0.6,"z":0.677,"el":"C"},{"x":2.792,"y":2.021,"